# Secrets for local development — loaded automatically by `aai dev`.
# Only variables listed here are available via ctx.env (not all of process.env).
#
# For production, use `aai secret put <NAME>` to set the same keys on the server.
# In both cases, access secrets in agent code via ctx.env.MY_KEY.
#
# --- The one key the default voice pipeline needs --------------------------
#
# `aai dev` runs speech-to-text, the LLM gateway and text-to-speech on a single
# AssemblyAI key, so this is the credential a session cannot start without.
# Any ONE of these is enough, and the first two need no aai account:
#
#   1. Paste your key after the `=` below.
#   2. Or export it in your shell: export ASSEMBLYAI_API_KEY=<your key>
#   3. Or run `aai login`, and `aai dev` will use your account's key.
#
# Get a key at https://www.assemblyai.com/dashboard.
#
# Leaving it blank is safe: a declared-but-empty value is dropped rather than
# handed to a provider, so options 2 and 3 still work with this line as it is.
ASSEMBLYAI_API_KEY=

# Add any other secrets your agent needs below:

# Required only if your agent enables the `web_search` builtin
# (free key: https://brave.com/search/api/):
# BRAVE_API_KEY=

# --- Durable workflows and uploads -----------------------------------------
#
# A DEPLOYED agent's runs are durable with no setup — the platform keeps them
# on its own database. `api.upload(file)` is the exception: an upload's record
# needs a database YOU supply, so without a DATABASE_URL the bytes live only as
# long as the sandbox even though the runs reading them do not.
#
# These four are the LOCAL equivalents, and none is needed by an agent that has
# no workflow.
#
# All three storage keys or none: two of three resolves to nothing and refuses
# by name rather than half-working. Nothing creates the bucket for you — a
# bucket is dashboard state, not a migration.
#
# From the Supabase CLI: `supabase start`, then `supabase status -o env` for
# API_URL and SERVICE_ROLE_KEY. The local stack declares one bucket, `blobs`,
# and uploads land under an `uploads/` prefix inside it — the same layout
# production uses beside its `blobs/<sha256>` deploy artifacts.
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres
# AAI_UPLOAD_STORAGE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
# AAI_UPLOAD_STORAGE_KEY=<SERVICE_ROLE_KEY>
# AAI_UPLOAD_STORAGE_BUCKET=blobs
